  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Everyone knows that Vrchat keeps being made fun of because of player performance, when in reality, a lot of the performance issue is from the Avatars (which can be improved still, but has been somewhat addressed already) and another big performance hitter are Worlds themselves. \nSo, my suggestion is to address worlds too, enforcing some basic world optimization techniques, like occlusion, GPU instancing, baking the shadows, and so on and forward. \nFor the experienced creators, its easy to notice a badly managed world, but for an average user, they will just blame the game itself...",
